<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sukkal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sukkal was a title of high office in ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>, originally meaning envoy or minister. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukkalmah-period">Sukkalmah period</a> the sukkal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a> was one of the three leading rulers. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a> describe this tripartite system of government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sukkal.jpg" alt="Sukkal" width="320" height="254" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis Delaporte (Loches, January 11, 1842 – Paris, May 3, 1925) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_Lugal-ushumgal_as_servant_of_Naram-Sin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
